    22	A transfer `{"from": X, "to": Y, "passengers": n}` says that `n` passengers who
    23	arrive on turn `X` leave on turn `Y`.
    24	
    25	`walk_metres[i][j]` is the walking distance, in metres, from the stand at
    26	position `i` of the `stands` list to the stand at position `j`. The day also
    27	gives `buffer_minutes` and `bus_cost_per_passenger`, and a list of
    28	`wingtip_pairs`: pairs of neighbouring stands whose wingtips would touch if
    29	both held a widebody.
    30	
    31	## What a plan must do
    32	
    33	Every turn of the day is on exactly one stand, and:
    34	
    35	1. The turn's `size` is at most the stand's `size`.
    36	2. An international turn is on a stand with `international` true. A turn that
    37	   is not international may use any stand.
    38	3. Two turns on the same stand keep apart by the buffer: one of them departs,
    39	   plus `buffer_minutes`, no later than the other arrives. A turn occupies its
    40	   stand from `arrive` to `depart`.
    41	4. For each pair in `wingtip_pairs`, the two stands never hold size-3 turns at
    42	   the same time: two such turns clash when each arrives before the other
    43	   departs. No buffer applies here, and turns smaller than size 3 never clash
    44	   this way.
    45	
    46	## Cost
    47	
    48	A plan costs the sum of:
    49	
    50	- for every turn on a remote stand, `bus_cost_per_passenger` times its
    51	  `pax_in` plus `pax_out`;
    52	- for every transfer, its `passengers` times `walk_metres` from the stand of
    53	  its `from` turn to the stand of its `to` turn.
    54	
    55	Costs are whole numbers, and lower is better. Where a turn sits on its stand
    56	does not matter beyond the rules above; nothing else is charged.
    57	
    58	## File format
    59	
    60	    {"stands": {"A01": ["T004", "T017", ...], "R02": [...], ...}}
    61	
    62	Each key is a stand id, given at most once; each list gives the ids of the turns
    63	on that stand as JSON strings, exactly as in the day file, in any order. A stand
    64	may be left out or given an empty list. Any other top-level key is ignored.

